{%- comment -%}
  Shared by snippets/5dla_product-card-1/2/3/4.liquid's badge logic.

  A `custom_badge` block on sections/5dla_collection-product-grid.liquid
  whose `product_list` includes this `product` overrides whatever badge
  text that card would otherwise show - product.metafields.custom.
  badge_text.value (card 1) or product.metafields.bwp_fields.badge_label
  (card 2/3/4), AND card 1's own "Sold out"/"Sale" fallback text - the
  badge's existing UI (markup/classes/conditional rendering) is untouched,
  only the TEXT is swapped. First matching block wins if more than one
  lists this product.

  Callers can't `assign` a snippet's local variable into their own scope,
  so this just echoes the override text (blank if none matches) for the
  caller to `capture` instead:

    {%- capture badge_override -%}
      {%- render '5dla_product-card-badge-override', product: product, section: section -%}
    {%- endcapture -%}
    {%- assign badge_override = badge_override | strip -%}
    {%- if badge_override != blank -%}{%- assign badge_text = badge_override -%}{%- endif -%}

  Expects: product, section
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- liquid
  assign override = ''
  for block in section.blocks
    if block.type == 'custom_badge' and block.settings.product_list contains product
      assign override = block.settings.label
      break
    endif
  endfor
-%}{{- override -}}
